  "hypothesis": "Equal-sized lexicographic rank intervals, statically shared by a persistent OpenMP team and formatted directly into an ordered output slab, can reduce scheduling, copying, and flushing overhead.",
  "notes": "Not executed. Preserves native character ordering, exact whitespace filtering, and output bytes. Sequential fallbacks cover small workloads, oversized records, count overflow, and builds without OpenMP.",
